WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.750
It's been a great year for television, but
unfortunately we can't say the same for many

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:06.880
of our favorite, dearly departed characters.

00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:11.320
That's why we're paying tribute to all the
TV characters who unexpectedly left us this

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:11.820
year.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.600
Be careful if you're not caught up on all
your favorite shows - from This is Us and

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.320
Walking Dead to Jessica Jones and even New
Girl.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:21.320
There are some major, major spoilers ahead.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:27.040
Millions of eager fans of NBC's smash hit
This Is Us knew that Pearson patriarch Jack

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:30.020
was going to die, but they weren't quite sure
how.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:34.480
On February 4, the show finally revealed exactly
how Jack passed away.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:40.120
In a flashback sequence set in 1998, we see
the family's slow cooker short out, sparking

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.540
a fire that quickly engulfs the Pearson home.

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:46.780
Jack wakes up in the middle of the night,
smells smoke, and turns into Hero Dad, getting

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:49.160
his family out of the house with a bedsheet
rope.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:52.860
Then he goes back into the burning house to
save Louie, the family dog.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:56.380
He's taken to the hospital to attend to minor
burns, and all seems well.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:57.440
Until:

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.739
"Your husband went into cardiac arrest.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:05.800
It was catastrophic and I'm afraid we've lost
him."

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:08.520
Carl Grimes grew up on TV.

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:13.380
The son of Walking Dead protagonist Rick Grimes,
Carl had been with the series since episode

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.220
one back in 2010.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:20.660
Along the way, he endures tragedies and setbacks,
including the death of his mother during childbirth,

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:24.340
the loss of an eye, and various acts of evil
by the show's villains.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:29.480
Keeping Carl alive and safe is the reason
Rick never completely crumbles, and Carl keeps

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:30.720
human decency alive.

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:35.760
Unfortunately, his luck comes to an end when
a zombie finally takes a bite out of Carl.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:39.580
It's a death sentence, but not an immediate
one, giving Carl time to say goodbye.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:44.930
He hangs out with his little sister Judith,
writes farewell letters, and then shoots himself

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:46.300
before he can go full walker.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:51.530
Carl wasn't the only Walking Dead character
whose death caught us by surprise - Simon

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:54.640
was Negan's loyal, selfless, and nasty second-in-command.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:58.560
What did he get for his constant devotion
to the evil leader of the Saviors?

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.620
Violently choked to death by his former boss.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.860
His death isn't completely out of the blue,
though...

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:08.780
Simon had been pretty brashly making some
overtures to take over the Sanctuary.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:13.520
Negan knows about it for a while, but rather
than kill Simon right away, he gives Simon

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.820
a few chances to prove himself or make it
right.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:20.599
Ultimately though, Simon's luck runs out when
Negan challenges him to a fight - with fatal

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:21.920
consequences for the loser.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:27.080
"You got saviors killed and then you ran away
like a coward.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:31.180
You got shown up one too many times."

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:37.280
NCIS wound down its 15th season with a heavily
promoted plot: The departure of original character

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:37.800
Abby.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:41.980
NCIS viewers worried that this news spelled
doom for the fan-favorite character.

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:46.920
It definitely didn't look good for Abby when
an episode ended with Abby and co-worker Clayton

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:48.880
Reeves seemingly shot by a mugger.

00:02:49.249 --> 00:02:53.420
Resolving that cliffhanger ending, next week's
episode found Ducky sympathizing with another

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:56.920
coroner about the agony of performing an autopsy
on a former colleague.

00:02:57.140 --> 00:02:58.700
Had Abby died from a gunshot?

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:00.520
[Sad music]

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:07.040
Surprise!

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:07.540
She hadn't.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:11.580
Instead it was Reeves who had died, having
selflessly stepped in front of Abby to take

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:12.080
the bullet.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:17.640
Despite surviving an attack by a serial killer
called the Black Hood earlier in the season,

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:22.100
Midge doesn't quite manage to make it through
the rest of Riverdale's second season alive.

00:03:22.109 --> 00:03:26.150
Her fate is sealed when she's cast in Riverdale
High's production of the musical version of

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:27.220
Stephen King's Carrie.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:32.450
When the curtain on the show rises, audiences
- and half the town of Riverdale - see a gruesome

00:03:32.450 --> 00:03:32.940
sight.

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:37.640
Midge, brutally stabbed, with creepy messages
written in blood on the wall around her.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.540
Midge may be gone, but she's definitely not
forgotten.

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:45.560
"The vixens and I vow that we will not rest
until those responsible for the murder of

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:48.500
our sister is rightly punished.”

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:53.140
Modern Family isn't the ratings juggernaut
it once was, and its tenth season may be one

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:53.780
of its last.

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:57.590
To bring back some of the viewers that have
tuned out over the years, the show pulled

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:02.060
a little publicity stunt before the season
began, promising that a "significant character"

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:03.780
would die an episode to come.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:08.180
Fans and reporters speculated about who would
be the one to kick the bucket - but no one

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:12.000
expected it to be DeDe, Jay's first wife and
Mitchell and Claire's mother.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:17.580
Deaths on Gotham are frequent, but the victims
are usually just underlings, stooges, or random

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:18.580
bystanders.

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:23.200
Shockingly, two major characters meet their
end in the show's fourth season finale.

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:27.620
Butch managed to cheat death once when he
was brought back to life in a toxic swamp,

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:32.280
but he's ultimately killed by the Penguin
as revenge for Butch's earlier murder of Penguin's

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:32.780
mother.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:37.360
Classic Batman villain Ra's al Ghul also bites
the big one in the season finale.

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:41.880
After Barbara turns down the baddie's offer
to leave Gotham, she stabs him in the chest

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:43.540
with the assistance of Bruce Wayne.

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:48.700
Will Simpson was a vital character in the
first season of Jessica Jones; first a cop

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:53.920
controlled by Kilgrave, then a love interest
for Trish Walker, and then, finally, an unstable

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:56.240
killer addicted to super-steroid-esque pills.

00:04:56.780 --> 00:04:59.480
When season 2 starts up, Simpson is stalking
Trish.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:04.360
He corners her and gets shot in the leg - at
which point he warns Trish that she's in danger.

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:08.820
A useful warning, but delivered a bit late,
since he's mysteriously killed minutes after

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:09.960
he delivers his warning."

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:14.980
Kimmy's tough-as-nails landlord Lillian found
love in the third season of Unbreakable Kimmy

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:18.950
Schmidt with Artie Goodman, the owner of a
Whole Foods-like grocery chain called Big

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:19.440
Naturals.

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:21.560
Nothing lasts forever, though.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:26.290
At the beginning of Season 4, viewers learn
that Artie died on their vacation, and Lillian

00:05:26.290 --> 00:05:30.500
was entrusted to spread his ashes at the site
of his summer camp in Manhattan, which had

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:32.180
turned into an exclusive club.

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:36.560
Barred from entering the club, Lillian is
able to give Artie the final resting place

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:41.610
he asked for, along with some closure for
herself: She sells two plastic baggies full

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:46.160
of Artie's cremated remains to a bunch of
finance-bros who clearly think those ashes

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:47.770
are something a little more party-friendly.

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:53.500
"This is the most fun I've had disposing of
a body since…

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:56.540
Well, just don't make me choose!"

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:59.440
If Scandal had to end, so would one of its
main characters.

00:05:59.940 --> 00:06:05.080
Somebody had to pay for seven seasons' worth
of political machinations, backstabbing, extramarital

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:07.940
affairs, politicking, terrorism, and murder.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:11.340
That person wound up being Attorney General
David Rosen.

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:16.260
In the penultimate episode, Washington, D.C.
fixer Olivia Pope tells the public about the

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:21.940
existence of the secretive B613 operation,
hoping that the revelation would somehow stop

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:24.140
sneaky, power-crazed Vice President Cyrus.

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:30.020
Unfortunately, that leads the increasingly
unhinged Cyrus to respond by poisoning Rosen

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:31.160
with a deadly cocktail.

00:06:31.480 --> 00:06:36.360
"David Rosen, you… are in my way.

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:38.800
No hard feelings."

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:46.240
The second season finale of the rebooted X-Files
killed off a lot of longtime characters.

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:51.400
One of the season's main arcs concerns Cigarette
Smoking Man's plans to unleash a deadly virus.

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:56.960
To pull it off, he manipulated Scully's shape-shifting
son William - along with FBI Assistant Director

00:06:56.960 --> 00:07:00.440
Walter Skinner and Agent Monica Reyes - into
helping him execute it.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:05.720
Smoking Man also happened to be William's
biological father - he was the one who'd drugged

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:08.840
and medically impregnated Scully nearly two
decades ago.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:13.580
William, wishing to be free of all this evil,
finally confronts his dad on a dock while

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:15.920
using his powers to disguise himself as Mulder.

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:21.100
Smoking Man shoots William-as-Mulder in the
head, right before the real Mulder arrives

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:23.380
to shoot Smoking Man and kick him into the
water.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:27.900
The deaths don't stop there; Skinner shoots
Agent Reyes, before getting run over by a

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:29.130
car himself.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:32.500
Luckily, it isn't all doom and gloom - William
seems to have survived.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:42.580
Fox's New Girl isn't so new anymore, and it
came to the end of its seven-season run with

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:46.870
a handful of episodes to wrap up all of its
loose ends and give each of its characters

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:47.860
a proper send-off.

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:51.100
Alas, a finale usually means somebody has
to die.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:56.460
And in this show's case, that somebody would
be Ferguson, the beloved smush-faced cat belonging

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:56.980
to Winston.

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:02.800
While viewers were saved the not-very-sitcom-friendly
images and emotional turmoil of watching a

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:08.380
pet die, New Girl devoted an episode to Winston's
over-the-top grieving process, which involves

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:12.600
a motorcade to an elaborate memorial service
conducted in the Jewish tradition.

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:14.780
We'll mourn you until we join you, Ferguson.

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:20.280
When the Tim Allen sitcom Last Man Standing
returned to Fox more than a year after ABC

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:22.480
canceled it, producers made a few changes.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:27.280
One of the biggest changes was that Bud Baxter,
portrayed by veteran character actor and Oscar

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:32.300
nominee Robert Forster, wouldn't be back at
all… because in the new season, Bud is dead.

00:08:32.830 --> 00:08:36.780
Forster shows up here and there on the ABC
version of the show, but producers used the

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:39.520
network switch to send his character to the
great beyond.

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:44.620
Luckily, Bud still got the opportunity to
appear one last time as a ghostly vision for

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:46.670
closure on some unresolved issues.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:48.500
"I tell my kids I love them all the time.

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:51.400
I don't think I ever remember you saying that."

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:59.740
In May 2018, Clayne Crawford was shockingly
fired from Fox's TV version of Lethal Weapon.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:04.920
Apparently, in his two seasons of work on
the show as loose-cannon cop Martin Riggs,

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:09.000
Crawford made life difficult on the set for
many people, notably co-star Damon Wayans.

00:09:09.749 --> 00:09:14.240
Prior to the third-season renewal, fans learned
that Crawford would be replaced by Seann William

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:17.340
Scott, who would play a new partner to Wayans'
Roger Murtaugh.

00:09:18.020 --> 00:09:22.360
That ramped up speculation as to how Lethal
Weapon would explain Crawford's sudden absence.

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:26.959
The show addressed the issue with its third-season
premiere, which found Riggs dying from a gunshot

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:29.140
wound he sustained in the second season cliffhanger.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:34.300
Of course, the body count of TV characters
doesn't end there...and, shocker, a few more

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:37.220
come from that zombie show where lots of people
die all the time.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:41.280
Here are some more familiar faces who went
off to that DVR in the sky...

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:44.740
Nick Clark - Fear the Walking Dead

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:48.019
Tobin - The Walking Dead

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:51.840
Spencer - American Housewife

00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:55.640
Madison - Fear the Walking Dead

00:09:57.840 --> 00:09:59.260
Gregory - The Walking Dead

